NAME = Apixaban_10CHCl3_XTB2_LooseOpt_from_confined_final.inp
|  1> # Apixaban + 10 CHCl3: XTB2 geometry optimization with LOOSENED convergence
|  2> # Starting geometry: final frame (Step 20000, t=20 ps) of the confined XTB2 MD
|  3> #   trajectory Apixaban_10CHCl3_XTB_preequil_confined.xyz
|  4> #   (Cell Sphere confinement, r=14.0 Ang)
|  5> #
|  6> # IMPORTANT DIFFERENCE FROM THE WATER/DMSO/MeOH VERSIONS:
|  7> #   This run intentionally uses LooseOpt convergence criteria instead of the
|  8> #   default (Normal) ones. The goal this time is different from before: we
|  9> #   want to relax each molecule's own internal strain from the raw MD
| 10> #   snapshot, WITHOUT letting solvent molecules that were clearly not yet
| 11> #   solvated at t=20ps drift further and start solvating during the
| 12> #   optimization itself. A tight/normal optimization tends to run many more
| 13> #   steps and lets those distant, weakly-bound CHCl3 molecules migrate toward
| 14> #   Apixaban over the course of the optimization (as seen with the water/MeOH
| 15> #   Opt runs). LooseOpt converges in far fewer steps, which should capture
| 16> #   "local relaxation only" and better preserve the actual solvation state
| 17> #   present at the end of the MD run.
| 18> #
| 19> # LooseOpt thresholds (looser than the ORCA default/Normal Opt by roughly
| 20> #   5-6x): TolE=3e-5, TolMaxG=2e-3, TolRMSG=5e-4, TolMaxD=1e-2, TolRMSD=7e-3
| 21> #
| 22> # Note: no SMD/solvent model and no Cell/confinement here - this is a plain
| 23> #   gas-phase XTB2 Opt of the whole 109-atom snapshot (Apixaban + 10 explicit
| 24> #   CHCl3).
| 25> 
| 26> ! XTB2 LooseOpt
| 27> 
| 28> %pal
| 29>   nprocs 4
| 30> end
| 31> 
| 32> %maxcore 2000
| 33> 
| 34> * xyz 0 1
